  "manual_review": {
    "gh5": "No pvc_mass_storage.c/h member in this entire official archive. The inspected f_mass_storage.c implements ordinary SCSI storage commands.",
    "s5m2": "The custom bridge copies a received 31-byte CBW, including its 16-byte CDB, into a structure exposed to local userspace by PVCUSB_GET_DATA. Its ioctl data transfer addresses are local userspace/driver fields, not demonstrated remote address-read commands.",
    "sequence_counter": "CurrentSerialNumber increments for a CBW and is checked on local ioctl replies. This is a transport sequence counter in the inspected driver, not evidence of camera pairing or a firmware decryption key.",
    "runtime_identity": "Default descriptor constants may be changed through PVCUSB_SET_DEV_DATA. Source defaults and presence in a release archive do not prove runtime binding, product IDs or behavior on any connected camera.",
    "missing_consumer": "The driver does not include the userspace consumer that assigns meaning to vendor CDBs. No arbitrary remote memory reader or GM5 command can be concluded from the forwarding interface."
  },
